From 220fb001a416fad36426bd994dd4e9a3e9ac681d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 08:35:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(corun): collapse to single predicate + state struct
 + JS API, split shadow_display_mode (PR-94 items 1-4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Maintainer feedback on the original co-run PR called out four structural
tightenings — none of them a redesign, just preventing future drift.

Item 1 — Single corun_event_owner() predicate. The let-through filter
at the sh_midi site and the suppress filter at the forward site each did
their own grp && !(keep_mask & grp) check, with a comment asking future
readers to keep them in sync. Collapsed both into one helper
corun_event_owner(ctrl, type, d1) -> {TOOL, PEER, BOTH, NONE} in
shadow_constants.h; each call site asks which side it is and switches on
the result. Drift impossible by construction.

Item 2 — Split the shadow_display_mode overload. Keeping
shadow_display_mode = 1 while early-returning from shadow_swap_display
during move_native worked, but it overloaded the field: future readers
of shadow_display_mode couldn't tell whether the shadow session was
active or whether Move firmware owned the OLED. Added a separate
shadow_display_owner field on shadow_control_t with a display_owner_t
enum (TOOL / SCHWUNG_UI / MOVE_FIRMWARE). shadow_display_mode reverts
to its literal meaning (shadow session armed vs not); the early-return
in shadow_swap_display now checks display_owner.

Item 3 — Collapse to one corun state field. The parallel int8_t
corun_chain_edit_slot + corun_move_native_track fields made "which one
do I check" a bug waiting to happen. Replaced with a single nested
struct { target, id, keep_mask } accessed via helpers corun_active(),
corun_target(), corun_id(), corun_keep_mask() in shadow_constants.h.
All read/write sites in schwung_shim.c, shadow_ui.c, and
shadow_led_queue.c go through the helpers; no direct field access
outside them. Adding a new co-run target = extend corun_target_t enum
and the predicate; nothing else to chase.

Item 4 — One JS entry point. Dropped the per-target setters
(shadow_set_corun_chain_edit / shadow_set_corun_move_native) and their
getters. Kept shadow_corun_begin(target, id, keep_mask) /
shadow_corun_end() / shadow_corun_state() — the last returns
{ target, id, keep_mask } or null, so tools can poll once per frame to
reconcile their own mirror. Registered the CORUN_TARGET_* and
CORUN_GRP_* enum values + CORUN_KEEP_DEFAULT as JS globals so tool code
doesn't have to redeclare them.

shadow_ui.js's tick-time reconcile rewritten to read shadow_corun_state()
once and switch on target. The chain editor's Back handler is unchanged
behaviorally (navigates within sub-views, silent at the top level — the
tool provides its own exit gesture); only the comment was generalized.

No functional regressions for the existing chain-edit / move-native
flows.
